  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="sub">
        App: <strong>THE Doctor At Home – Doctors</strong><br>
        Publisher: <strong>The Doctor At Home</strong><br>
        Effective date: <strong>2025-09-14</strong> &nbsp;•&nbsp; Last updated: <strong>2025-09-14</strong>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>1) Scope</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy applies to our doctor-facing Android app “THE Doctor At Home – Doctors” and its connected backend services. The app helps doctors manage patient home visits/consultations, appointments, payment settlements, and support. It is not intended for emergency use.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2) What data we collect & why</h2>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Account & Profile</td>
          <td>Name, phone, email, profile photo, specialty, clinic info</td>
          <td>Account creation, verification, in-app identification, receipts</td>
          <td>Active account life; legal/audit duties as needed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Consultation & Scheduling</td>
          <td>Appointments, visit slots, basic case notes you enter</td>
          <td>Scheduling, record-keeping for continuity of care you provide</td>
          <td>As required for operations/legal compliance; deletion requests where legally allowed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Payments</td>
          <td>UPI/wallet intent ref, transaction IDs, status (we do not store card data)</td>
          <td>Collections, refunds, settlements, invoices</td>
          <td>As required by tax/audit laws</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Device & App Diagnostics</td>
          <td>Device model, OS/app version, crash logs, performance events</td>
          <td>Reliability, debugging, security</td>
          <td>Short-term operational windows</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Location <span class="pill">optional</span></td>
          <td>Approximate/precise location if you allow</td>
          <td>Route/ETA for home visits; service area checks</td>
          <td>Real-time use; not stored continuously</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Support Communications</td>
          <td>In-app messages, tickets, call metadata, push token</td>
          <td>Customer support, notifications</td>
          <td>Life of ticket/need; per law</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3) Android permissions & usage</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION / ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION</code> (optional): nearby match & on-the-way updates for visits.</li>
        <li><code>POST_NOTIFICATIONS</code>: appointment reminders, payment/settlement alerts.</li>
        <li><code>CAMERA / READ_MEDIA_IMAGES</code>: capture/upload prescriptions, reports, profile photos (only when you choose).</li>
        <li><code>READ/WRITE EXTERNAL STORAGE</code> (if applicable on your OS version): create/download invoices you request.</li>
        <li><code>CALL_PHONE</code> (optional): click-to-call patient/helpline (no call logs accessed).</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">You can change or revoke these permissions anytime in Android Settings. Some features may be limited if disabled.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4) How we use your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide core features: bookings, home visits, consult records, payouts.</li>
        <li>Send transactional updates (appointments, payments, account/security).</li>
        <li>Prevent fraud/abuse; comply with law and platform policies.</li>
        <li>Diagnostics & analytics to improve stability and user experience.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5) Sharing & disclosure</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal data.</li>
        <li>We share with: (a) patients connected to your profile as required for care; (b) service providers (hosting, analytics/crash, maps/location, payments) under contracts; (c) competent authorities when legally required; (d) in case of business reorganization with safeguards.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Sub-processors / services (examples)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Google Firebase (Analytics & Crashlytics)</li>
        <li>Google Maps/Location Services</li>
        <li>Payment gateway / UPI PSP (for intents & settlement metadata)</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6) Your choices & rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Access/update profile & clinic details in the app.</li>
        <li>Download invoices/records where available, or request via support.</li>
        <li>Delete account: <span class="kbd">App &gt; Profile &gt; Account &gt; Delete Account</span> (or request via support). We may retain some records required by law (e.g., tax/audit).</li>
        <li>Control notifications & permissions in Android Settings.</li>
        <li>Additional rights under applicable laws (e.g., GDPR/UK, California) – access, rectification, objection, portability, etc. We honor them as per law.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7) Security</h2>
      <p>We use transport-level encryption, access controls, and data minimization principles. No method is 100% secure, but we continuously improve security measures.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8) Children</h2>
      <p>This app is intended for licensed adult doctors. It is not for individuals under 18 years of age.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9) International transfers</h2>
      <p>Data may be processed on servers located inside or outside your country. Where required, we implement appropriate safeguards (e.g., standard contractual clauses).</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10) Data retention & deletion</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We retain data only as long as needed for services and legal purposes.</li>
        <li>Upon a verified deletion request, we will erase or anonymize data except records legally required to be retained (e.g., tax, audit, disputes).</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11) Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this Policy from time to time. Important changes will be notified in-app, via email, or on our website. Continued use of the service after updates means acceptance of the new Policy.</p>
    </section>

